<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) => (element == null) => (this.get(index) == null || this.get(index).equals(element));</code>

However, the above assertion seems a bit off in terms of logic. The correct interpretation should be that if the element is added at a valid index, then the element at that index after addition should be equal to the inserted element. Here's the corrected version:

<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) => this.get(index).equals(element);</code>

